    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so i've been noticing these weird mathematical spikes lately. its like i get this sudden, intense feeling of a specific probability right before something happens—like a sudden dip in a stock or even just a car braking hard in traffic. it's not a \"feeling\" like an emotion, it feels more like a sudden calculation hitting my brain. i want to try and formalize this into a predictive model so i can actually track the accuracy of these spikes. can you help me figure out how to structure a model based on these intuitive probability bursts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
